    <time>1786461340</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.27.0: Kimi K3 and Qwen3.5 model support, FlashAttention 4 FP8 KV cache on SM100, DeepSeek-V4 performance work, Model Runner V2 for non-generative workloads, Arm INT8 fused MoE CPU kernel, and a gRPC control plane in the Rust frontend. Raises the python-mistral-common floor to &gt;= 1.11.6 per upstream; both patches rebased. Plamo2/Ouro models and max_num_partial_prefills/max_long_partial_prefills removed upstream. Built green locally on aarch64 for both multibuild flavours (default and cpu), import smoke test passes against Factory's torch 2.12.0.</comment>
    <requestid>1370608</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="7" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>1ffd972f93f26583923fdd2d96bfbf90</srcmd5>
    <version>0.27.1</version>
    <time>1786543947</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.27.1

Upstream point release. Only 7 files differ from 0.27.0 -- version strings, a
Dockerfile, buildkite config and one model file -- and pyproject.toml,
requirements/ and cmake/cpu_extension.cmake are byte-identical, so no
dependency floors and no oneDNN or ACL pins needed touching. Both downstream
patches apply unchanged.

One packaging change beyond the version. The spec carried an exact
&quot;Requires: python-compressed-tensors = 0.17.1&quot;, which would have made this
package uninstallable as soon as compressed-tensors 0.18.0 landed. That is
now a floor, &quot;&gt;= 0.17.1&quot;. A floor rather than &quot;&gt;= 0.18.0&quot; is deliberate:
vLLM upstream still pins compressed-tensors == 0.17.0, so demanding 0.18.0
would assert a minimum upstream does not require and would make this
unresolvable until the companion submission is in. As written, the two are
order-independent.

The 15 symbols vllm imports from compressed_tensors were checked against both
0.17.1 and 0.18.0: all present in both, nothing removed, one purely additive
change. Note compressed-tensors is not a BuildRequires here, so that evidence
is static rather than exercised by the build.

Verified on aarch64, both multibuild flavours built natively: the default
flavour (VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=empty) and the cpu flavour
(VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu), each green and each reporting 0.27.1 from the
import smoke test.

Worth flagging for a future cleanup rather than this submission: the spec
still carries several other exact pins mirroring upstream's ==, namely depyf,
lm-format-enforcer, outlines_core and torch. Each is the same latent
breakage whenever the devel project moves one of them.</comment>
    <requestid>1370785</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="8" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>66fa1c6c1bd629d46188e2ae6d748b23</srcmd5>
    <version>0.28.0</version>
    <time>1787849502</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>python-vllm 0.28.0

Update to upstream 0.28.0, plus the dependency-pin cleanup this package
has owed for a while.

All remaining exact &quot;=&quot; version requirements are converted to &quot;&gt;=&quot;
floors at the version upstream actually asks for:

  python-torch              = 2.12.0  -&gt;  &gt;= 2.12.0
  python-depyf              = 0.20.0  -&gt;  &gt;= 0.20.0
  python-lm-format-enforcer = 0.11.3  -&gt;  &gt;= 0.11.3
  python-outlines_core      = 0.2.14  -&gt;  &gt;= 0.2.14

plus the matching torch / torch-devel BuildRequires. An exact RPM pin
couples two independently released packages, so every update of either
leaves the other uninstallable, and nothing catches it because it only
fails at install time. depyf, lm-format-enforcer and outlines_core are
lazily imported optional backends and all three are currently at their
latest upstream release, so each floor is exactly upstream's own pin.
For the cpu flavour the link against torch is already expressed by the
automatic libtorch.so / libtorch_cpu.so / libc10.so dependencies rpm
generates from the compiled extension. No exact pin was kept.
vllm-relax-cpu-requirements.patch relaxes the same pins in the wheel
metadata so the RPM dependencies and the installed dist-info agree.

Also in this request:
  - python-huggingface-hub &gt;= 1.27.0, a new upstream floor in 0.28.0
  - oneDNN 3.13 on x86_64, following upstream's cmake/cpu_extension.cmake
    (the aarch64 commit pin and Arm Compute Library 52.6.0 are unchanged)
  - switched from update-alternatives to libalternatives

Built and tested natively on aarch64, both multibuild flavours.</comment>
    <requestid>1373880</requestid>
  </revision>
